---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /syllabus/
title: Syllabus
subtitle: A dependency-ordered map from foundations to the frontier.
eyebrow: The map
description: The complete 180-day course map, with published lessons linked as they arrive.
---

{% set totalDays = syllabus | totalSyllabusDays %}
{% set publishedCount = collections.days | publishedCount %}
{% set nextDay = syllabus | nextSyllabusDay(collections.days) %}
{% set upcoming = syllabus | upcomingSyllabusDays(collections.days, 6) %}

<p class="lede">The syllabus is the book's route through the world: not a shelf of unrelated topics, but a sequence of descents where each day gives the next one firmer ground. It begins by asking how belief earns trust, then moves through mathematics, physics, chemistry, life, medicine, mind, artificial intelligence, economics, societies, ethics, and the future.</p>

<p>Every lesson keeps the same internal shape: an accessible entry point, a core model, a live debate, and a walk toward recent research. The frontier is treated with discipline. Claims are marked as established, promising hints, or contested hype; the goal is not to make novelty feel certain, but to show how evidence changes its weight.</p>

<div class="syllabus-progress" aria-label="Syllabus progress">
  <div>
    <p class="progress-label">Published now</p>
    <p class="progress-number">{{ publishedCount }} of {{ totalDays }} days</p>
  </div>
  {% if nextDay %}
  <div>
    <p class="progress-label">Next descent</p>
    <p class="progress-next">Day {{ nextDay.day | padDay }} · {{ nextDay.title }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<nav class="syllabus-block-nav" aria-label="Syllabus blocks">
{% for block in syllabus.blocks %}
  <a href="#block-{{ block.id | lower }}">Block {{ block.id }}</a>
{% endfor %}
</nav>

{% for block in syllabus.blocks %}
<section class="syllabus-block" id="block-{{ block.id | lower }}">
  <p class="sec-eyebrow">Block {{ block.id }} · Days {{ block.start_day }}-{{ block.end_day }}</p>
  <h2>{{ block.title }}</h2>
  <p>{{ block.summary }}</p>

  <div class="syllabus-days">
  {% for day in block.days %}
    {% set published = collections.days | publishedItemForDay(day.day) %}
    <article class="day-card syllabus-card{% if published %} is-published{% endif %}">
      <p class="card-kicker">Day {{ day.day | padDay }} / {{ book.total_days }}{% if not published %} · Planned{% endif %}</p>
      <h3>
      {% if published %}
        <a href="{{ published.url }}">{{ published.data.title }}</a>
      {% else %}
        {{ day.title }}
      {% endif %}
      </h3>
      {% if published %}
      <p>{{ published.data.summary }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </article>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section class="next-summary" aria-labelledby="what-comes-next">
  <p class="sec-eyebrow">Continuation</p>
  <h2 id="what-comes-next">What Comes Next</h2>
  {% if nextDay %}
  <p>The book has published through Day {{ publishedCount | padDay }}. The next lesson is <strong>Day {{ nextDay.day | padDay }}: {{ nextDay.title }}</strong>, in Block {{ nextDay.block_id }}. It continues the opening toolkit by sharpening the difference between valid inference, strong evidence, and persuasive error.</p>
  <ol class="upcoming-list">
  {% for day in upcoming %}
    <li><span class="upcoming-day">Day {{ day.day | padDay }} · </span><span>{{ day.title }}</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  <p>After these opening moves, the course turns from how we know to the formal languages of knowledge: probability, information, systems, mathematics, and computation. Those tools become the launch rail for the later descents into physical law, living systems, minds, institutions, and the research frontier.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>All 180 descents have been published. The next work is maintenance: tightening links, refreshing frontier claims, and keeping the evidence labels current as the research record changes.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
